    <http://example.org/node/chunk84> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's certifications, the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR)frameworks (the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), EU AI Act, RGS, SecNumCloud, NIS2) as of 2024, what are the security and compliance measures for this project?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk85> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that our company's have the necessary certifications and instruments to guarantee strict compliance with the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). our company's standard data residency is the European Union only, and our company's cross-border transfer policy prohibits data transfer outside the European Union unless there is an explicit legal basis.  our company's have anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to protect sensitive data. our company's also implement data subject rights including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. our company's Data Protection Officer can be contacted at dpo@nexus-engineering.it." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk86> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explicability and transparency, our company's AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. our company's also have model isolation in place, allowing only inference API access to end users, with no direct model access.  our company's audit capabilities include logging all queries, using an append-only method with SHA-256 hash chaining for log immutability, and retaining audit logs for 7 years. our company's also have real-time SIEM integration using tools like Wazuh and Elastic SIEM." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk87> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's experience with the European Union regulatory frameworks including the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR), EU AI Act, RGS v2, SecNumCloud, NIS2 Directive, and eIDAS as of 2024, our company's can ensure that the solution is designed and operated in compliance with these regulations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk88> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company's ISO 27001 certification, which includes the scope of design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, demonstrates our company's commitment to information security management. our company's risk management approach, aligned with ISO 27001, also ensures that our company's identify and mitigate potential risks. our company's will conduct a Data Protection Impact Assessment (DPIA) for this project, which typically takes around 3 weeks to complete, to identify and assess any potential data protection risks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk89> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In summary, our company's security and compliance measures for this project include strict the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) compliance, the European Union data hosting, no cross-border data transfer, anonymisation of sensitive data, explicability and transparency of AI-driven recommendations, robust audit capabilities, and adherence to the European Union regulatory frameworks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
